o rise","d":"2026-10-08","pol":1,"sig":0.68,"tier":"low","why":"effort to rise with a result: professional money not selling","ref":null},"key_bars":[{"name":"No supply","d":"2026-07-23","pol":1,"sig":0.98,"tier":"moderate"},{"name":"No supply","d":"2026-08-12","pol":1,"sig":0.98,"tier":"moderate"},{"name":"Test in a rising market","d":"2026-08-13","pol":1,"sig":1.4,"tier":"high"},{"name":"Test","d":"2026-08-17","pol":1,"sig":0.98,"tier":"moderate"},{"name":"Test","d":"2026-08-21","pol":1,"sig":1.12,"tier":"moderate"},{"name":"Effort to rise","d":"2026-10-08","pol":1,"sig":0.68,"tier":"low"}],"asof":null},"scores":{"overall":53,"group":"SIC 283x (Chemicals & Pharma)","group_rank":97,"group_n":238,"sector_rank":148,"sector_n":375,"earn":18}},"biz":{"name":"TAKEDA PHARMACEUTICAL CO LTD","desc":"Takeda Pharmaceutical Company Limited engages in the research, development, manufacture, marketing, and out-licensing of pharmaceutical products. It offers pharmaceutical products in the areas of gastroenterology, rare diseases, plasma-derived therapies, oncology, vaccines, and neuroscience. The company provides its products under the Entyvio, Gattex/Revestive, Takecab/Vocinti, EOHILIA, Takhzyro, Advate, Elaprase, Replagal, Vpriv, Adynovate/Adynovi, Livtencity, ADZYNMA, Gammagard Liquid/Kiovig, Hyqvia, Cuvitru, Flexbumin, Adcetris, Leuplin/Enantone, Ninlaro, Iclusig, FRUZAQLA, Alunbrig, vyvanse/elvanse, Trintellix, and QDENGA brands. It has licensing and collaboration for the development and commercialization of products with Arrowhead Pharmaceuticals, Cour Pharmaceuticals, Engitix, Halozyme, Mirum Pharmaceuticals, Ucsd/Fortis Advisors, Zedira/Dr. Falk Pharma, Ac Immune, Acurastem, Anima Biotech, Biomarin, Denali Therapeutics, Luxna Biotech, Neurocrine Biosciences, Peptidream, Abbvie, Adimab, Ascentage Pharma, Crescendo Biologics, Exelixis, F-Star, Gsk, Heidelberg Pharma, Innovent Biologics, Keros Therapeutics, Kumquat Biosciences, Protagonist Therapeutics, Halozyme, Kamada, Johnson & Johnson/Momenta Pharmaceuticals, Previpharma, Novavax, Bridgene Biosciences, Charles River Laboratories, Iambic Therapeutics, Ipsen, Km Biologics, Massachusetts Institute Of Technology, and Nabla Bio. The company operates in Japan, the United States. Europe, Canada, Latin America, China, Asia, Russia/Commonwealth of Independent States, the Middle East, Oceania, and Africa. The company was founded in 1781 and is headquartered in Chuo, Japan.","desc_src":"Yahoo Finance profile via yfinance (third-party)","sic":"2834","sic_desc":"Pharmaceutical Preparations","sector":"Healthcare","industry":"Drug Manufacturers - Specialty & Generic","mcap":60229468160,"mcap_src":"Yahoo Finance profile (third-party, cached)","hq":"TOKYO, Japan","exchange":"XNYS","cik":1395064,"massive_note":"Massive ticker details not fetched yet (5 calls/min limit; filled in on a nightly run)","sec_asof":"2026-10-08"},"fin":{"available":true,"src":"Yahoo quarterly income statement via yfinance (third-party fallback)","asof":"2026-10-06","q":[{"end":"2025-06-30","rev":1106685000000.0,"rev_yoy":null,"eps":39.115,"eps_yoy":null,"ni":124243000000.0,"ni_yoy":null,"nm":11.2,"derived":null,"fp":null},{"end":"2025-09-30","rev":1112796000000.0,"rev_yoy":null,"eps":null,"eps_yoy":null,"ni":-11802000000.0,"ni_yoy":null,"nm":-1.1,"derived":null,"fp":null},{"end":"2025-12-31","rev":1191698000000.0,"rev_yoy":null,"eps":null,"eps_yoy":null,"ni":103640000000.0,"ni_yoy":null,"nm":8.7,"derived":null,"fp":null},{"end":"2026-03-31","rev":1094541000000.0,"rev_yoy":null,"eps":null,"eps_yoy":null,"ni":-368471000000.0,"ni_yoy":null,"nm":-33.7,"derived":null,"fp":null},{"end":"2026-06-30","rev":1219900000000.0,"rev_yoy":10.2,"eps":35.27,"eps_yoy":-9.8,"ni":113197000000.0,"ni_yoy":-8.9,"nm":9.3,"derived":null,"fp":null}],"a":[{"end":"2020-03-31","rev":3291188000000.0,"rev_yoy":null,"eps":28.25,"eps_yoy":null,"ni":44290000000.0,"nm":1.3},{"end":"2021-03-31","rev":3197812000000.0,"rev_yoy":-2.84,"eps":238.96,"eps_yoy":745